    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Alternate title : A world of lyrics.  This file contains Pippin's English translations for arias from multiple operas along with texts for introductory and linking narrations and, in some cases, graphics of music notation for the first lines of the arias.  At the end of the document is list of operas that Pippin has translated to English.  \r\n\r\nArias included are from the following operas: Marriage of Figaro/Mozart -- Don Giovanni/Mozart -- Cosi fan tutte (The way of women)/Mozart -- Abduction from the seraglio=Yanked from the harem/Mozart -- Magic flute/Mozart -- Barber of Seville/Rossini -- Cenerentola=Cinderella/Rossini -- Italian girl in Algeria/Rossini -- Count Ory/Rossini -- Elixir of love/Donizetti -- Don Pasquale/Donizetti -- Lucia di Lammermoor/Donizetti -- Lucrezia Borgia/Donizetti -- Macbeth/Verdi -- Rigoletto/Verdi -- Traviata/Verdi -- Falstaff/Verdi -- Halka/Moniuszko -- Haunted manor/Moniuszko -- Orpheus in the underworld/Offenbach -- Belle Helene/Offenbach -- Vie Parisienne/Offenbach  -- Bandits/Offenbach -- Bridge of sighs : Carnival in Venice/Offenbach -- Perichole/Offenbach -- Princess of Trebizonde/Offenbach -- Bluebeard/Offenbach -- Tales of Hoffman/Offenbach -- Bartered bride/Smetana -- Two widows/Smetana -- Carmen/Bizet -- Eugene Onegin/Tchaikovsky -- Queen of Spades/Tchaikovsky -- Manon/Massenet -- Boheme/Puccini -- Madame Butterfly/Puccini -- Tosca/Puccini -- Manon Lescaut/Puccini -- Rondine=The swallow/Puccini -- Merry widow/Lehar -- Cunning little vixen/Janacek.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
